path: /attendance
title: School attendance software that works with no internet
description: A daily class register marked from a phone that keeps working when the internet drops. Finalise the day, lock it, and print the monthly sheet.
nav: Attendance
nav_order: 2
breadcrumb: Attendance
schema: org software
priority: 0.9
---

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Attendance</span>
    <h1>The register, marked in the classroom</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width:62ch">
      A teacher opens their class on a phone, taps the two or three children who
      are not there, and presses save. That is the whole interaction, and it has
      to be faster than the paper register or it will not be used.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__cta">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/pricing" data-app="signup">Start 14 day free trial</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/guide.html">Read the handbook</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>It keeps working when the connection does not</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:64ch">
      This is the part most software gets wrong, and the part that decides
      whether teachers keep using it in week three.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:34px">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Marked offline, queued, then synced</h3>
        <p>
          A register marked with no signal is saved on the phone and sent when
          there is one. The teacher is told which state it is in rather than left
          guessing, and the same class cannot be marked twice into two different
          answers.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Finalise and lock the day</h3>
        <p>
          An unfinalised register is a draft and says so. Once the day is
          finalised it is locked, so a figure quoted to a parent in the afternoon
          is the same figure next week. A correction after that is a recorded
          change, not a silent overwrite.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Teachers see only their own classes</h3>
        <p>
          A teacher login reaches the classes and subjects that teacher actually
          teaches, and nothing else. That is enforced in the database rather than
          by hiding a menu, so it holds even if somebody types a different
          address.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The printable monthly sheet</h3>
        <p>
          The sheet an inspector or a board asks for, printed from the same data
          the teachers marked, so it cannot disagree with itself. Present,
          absent, late, half day and leave are all separate states.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <h2>Attendance is also a fee control</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">
        A pupil who is on the fee roll but has never appeared in any attendance
        register is worth looking at. That is not an accusation, it is usually a
        pupil who left and was never marked as gone, and it is money the school
        thinks it is owed by a family that has moved on.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:16px">
        The reconciliation screen puts those two lists side by side and names the
        difference, which is a check no paper register can do at all.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:20px">
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/fee-management">How the fee side works</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head">
        <span class="panel__title">Class 5 A</span>
        <span class="panel__sub">Thursday, 3 September</span>
      </div>
      <div class="app__rows" style="border:0;border-radius:0">
        <div class="arow"><span>Ahmed Raza</span><span class="pill pill--paid">Present</span></div>
        <div class="arow"><span>Fatima Bibi</span><span class="pill pill--paid">Present</span></div>
        <div class="arow"><span>Bilal Ahmad</span><span class="pill pill--due">Absent</span></div>
        <div class="arow"><span>Ayesha Noor</span><span class="pill pill--due">Late</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel__foot">
        38 present, 2 absent, 1 late. Finalised at 09:14 by Miss Saima.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

